{
  "case": "tombstones/003-bucket-scoped-delete",
  "cites": [
    "P:keyset-pagination-and-delivery-bound",
    "P:mutations-and-column-masked-conflict-resolution",
    "P:cursor-monotonicity-rebase-and-atomic-checkpoints"
  ],
  "context": {
    "client_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-c10000000001",
    "notes": [
      "Tombstone PKs are bucket-scoped like live row images: a pull whose params do not match the stored bucket snapshot must not observe the deleted PK, while the cursor still advances (P:keyset-pagination-and-delivery-bound).",
      "Empty params on a bucketed table are refused (pull policy `KZL01`): tombstones carry only the stored bucket snapshot and never replay RLS, so a vacuous match would leak every deleted pk. Unbucketed tables stay table-scoped.",
      "The wire tombstone remains { deleted_at, pk, seq, table }, with no snapshot key. RLS stricter than the bucket is not replayed on a gone row."
    ],
    "schema_version": 1,
    "server": {
      "min_schema_version": 1,
      "tables": {
        "todos": {
          "bucket_column": "owner_id"
        }
      },
      "tombstone_ttl_days": 30
    },
    "user_id": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-a10000000001"
  },
